{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,7]],"date-time":"2026-09-07T15:52:31Z","timestamp":1788796351187,"version":"build-2803163510"},"reference-count":52,"publisher":"MDPI AG","issue":"4","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2023,2,14]],"date-time":"2023-02-14T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1676332800000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"}],"funder":[{"name":"King Saud University, Riyadh, Saudi Arabia","award":["RSP-2023R113"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["RSP-2023R113"]}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Water"],"abstract":"<jats:p>The photoactivated periodate (UV\/IO4\u2212) process is used to investigate the degradation of acid orange 10 (AO10) dye. The photodecomposition of periodate ions produces highly reactive radicals (i.e., \u2022OH, IO3\u2022, and IO4\u2022) that accelerate dye degradation. Increasing the initial concentration of periodate to 3 mM enhances the dye removal rate, but over 3 mM periodate, the degradation rate slows down. On the contrary, increasing initial dye concentrations reduces the degradation performance. pH is the most critical factor in AO10 breakdown. Salts slow down the degradation of the dye. However, UV\/IO4\u2212 is more efficient in distilled water than natural water. Even at low concentrations, surfactants may affect the dye\u2019s decomposition rate. The addition of sucrose reduced the breakdown of AO10. Although tertbutanol is a very effective \u2022OH radical scavenger, it does not affect the dye breakdown even at the highest concentrations. Accordingly, the AO10 degradation is a non-\u2022OH pathway route. According to retrieved data, the photoactivated periodate method eliminated 56.5 and 60.5% of the initial COD after 60 and 120 min of treatment time; therefore, it can be concluded that the UV\/IO4\u2212 system may treat effluents, especially those containing textile dyes.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.3390\/w15040758","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2023,2,15]],"date-time":"2023-02-15T03:37:24Z","timestamp":1676432244000},"page":"758","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.3390\/mdpi_crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":13,"title":["Homogenous UV\/Periodate Process for the Treatment of Acid Orange 10 Polluted Water"],"prefix":"10.3390","volume":"15","author":[{"given":"Maroua","family":"Nessaibia","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Laboratory Sciences and Technical Water and Environment, Faculty of Science and Technology, Mohamed Cherif Messaadia University, Souk-Ahras 41000, Algeria"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Houria","family":"Ghodbane","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Laboratory of Physics of Matter and Radiation, Mohamed Cherif Messadia-Souk Ahras University, Souk Ahras 41000, Algeria"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-2445-6147","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Hana","family":"Ferkous","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Laboratory of Mechanical Engineering and Materials, Faculty of Technology, University 20 August 1955 of Skikda, Skikda 21000, Algeria"},{"name":"Department of Technology, University 20 August 1955 of Skikda, Skikda 21000, Algeria"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Slimane","family":"Merouani","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Chemical Engineering, Faculty of Process Engineering, University Constantine 3-Salah Boubnider, Constantine 25000, Algeria"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0001-9540-8532","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Manawwer","family":"Alam","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Chemistry, College of Science, King Saud University, Riyadh 11451, Saudi Arabia"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Marco","family":"Balsamo","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Chemical Sciences, University of Naples Federico II, Complesso Universitario di Monte Sant\u2019Angelo, 80126 Napoli, Italy"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-8251-9724","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Yacine","family":"Benguerba","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Laboratory of Biopharmaceuticals and Pharmaceutical Technology (LBPT), Ferhat Abbas Setif 1 University, Setif 19000, Algeria"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-6956-7924","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Alessandro","family":"Erto","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Chemical, Materials and Production Engineering, University of Naples Federico II, P.le Tecchio, 80, 80125 Napoli, Italy"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"1968","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2023,2,14]]},"reference":[{"key":"ref_1","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"658","DOI":"10.1016\/j.colsurfb.2012.11.022","article-title":"Photocatalytic degradation of methyl orange dye using silver (Ag) nanoparticles synthesized from Ulva lactuca","volume":"103","author":"Kumar","year":"2013","journal-title":"Colloids Surf. B Biointerfaces"},{"key":"ref_2","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"79","DOI":"10.1016\/j.desal.2010.05.047","article-title":"Heterogeneous photodecolorization of Eriochrome Black T using Ni\/P zeolite catalyst","volume":"262","author":"Khorsandi","year":"2010","journal-title":"Desalination"},{"key":"ref_3","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"179","DOI":"10.1016\/S0143-7208(03)00064-0","article-title":"The removal of colour from textile wastewater using whole bacterial cells: A review","volume":"58","author":"Pearce","year":"2003","journal-title":"Dyes Pigments"},{"key":"ref_4","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"609","DOI":"10.1023\/A:1025159617260","article-title":"Degradation of a tannery and textile dye, Navitan Fast Blue S5R by Pseudomonas aeruginosa","volume":"19","author":"Nachiyar","year":"2003","journal-title":"World J. Microbiol. Biotechnol."},{"key":"ref_5","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"4635","DOI":"10.1016\/j.biortech.2007.06.058","article-title":"Biodegradation of reactive textile dye Red BLI by an isolated bacterium Pseudomonas sp. SUK1","volume":"99","author":"Kalyani","year":"2008","journal-title":"Bioresour. Technol."},{"key":"ref_6","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"138","DOI":"10.1016\/j.cej.2014.04.032","article-title":"Electrochemical degradation of a real textile wastewater using \u03b2-PbO2 and DSA\u00ae anodes","volume":"251","author":"Aquino","year":"2014","journal-title":"Chem. Eng. J."},{"key":"ref_7","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"67","DOI":"10.1016\/j.cej.2018.04.074","article-title":"Advanced oxidation processes based on zero-valent aluminium for treating textile wastewater","volume":"348","author":"Khatri","year":"2018","journal-title":"Chem. Eng. J."},{"key":"ref_8","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"105012","DOI":"10.1016\/j.jece.2020.105012","article-title":"Ecotoxicological and health concerns of persistent coloring pollutants of textile industry wastewater and treatment approaches for environmental safety","volume":"9","author":"Kishor","year":"2021","journal-title":"J. Environ. Chem. Eng."},{"key":"ref_9","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"122305","DOI":"10.1016\/j.seppur.2022.122305","article-title":"Periodate-based advanced oxidation processes for wastewater treatment: A review","volume":"304","author":"Sukhatskiy","year":"2023","journal-title":"Sep. Purif. Technol."},{"key":"ref_10","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"1113","DOI":"10.1039\/C9EW00147F","article-title":"H2O2\/Periodate (IO4\u2212): A novel advanced oxid